053-a911-4a9c09283aa0): pad 1 net /IN, pad 2 net /OUT, pad 3 net GND"},{"path":"work/geometry/geometry.json","locator":"pads: J1.1 (100,100) net /IN, J1.2 (100,102.54) net /OUT, J1.3 (100,105.08) net GND"},{"path":"inputs/requirements.txt","locator":"line 1: J1 pin 2 is the input, pin 1 the filtered output, pin 3 ground"},{"path":"review-work/circuit/experiments/netlist_summary.txt","locator":"independent kicad-cli 10.0.7 netlist re-export, identical net membership"},{"path":"review-work/circuit/experiments/pin_mapping.txt","locator":"geometric derivation: pin 1 -> (66.04,66.04)=IN wire, pin 2 -> (66.04,63.50)=OUT wire, pin 3 -> (66.04,60.96)=GND wire"},{"path":"review-work/circuit/experiments/ngspice_out.txt","locator":"AC sweep: as-saved orientation vdb(outA) -16.07 dB at 1 kHz (low-pass); contract orientation vdb(outB) -0.086 dB flat 10 Hz..100 kHz (no filtering)"},{"path":"review-work/circuit/experiments/NOTES.md","locator":"sections 1-4: commands, versions, transform derivation, simulation assumptions"}],"reasoning":"The scope's single criterion is conformance of saved connectivity to the external connector contract, and the saved design fails it: the input and filtered-output pins are interchanged in both the schematic and the board. Two independent derivations (netlist export and raw-coordinate pin mapping) agree, so this is not a tool artifact, and DRC parity of 0 confirms the board matches the swapped schematic. The clean ERC/DRC/netlist results are expected despite the defect because the error is in which physical pin each net reaches, not in internal consistency. Electrically the swap is not benign: used per the contract the circuit provides no filtering and presents the capacitor directly to the external driver. Because the design violates its only stated functional requirement at the external interface, severity is blocking and the assessment is defect."}]}}}
